# Everything is excluded, then the build inputs are added back. A denylist quietly
# grows holes -- a new directory of local state is included by default and nobody
# notices until it is in a published image.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!backend/
!scripts/
# The console's sources. The image builds them in its own stage; see the
# Dockerfile. Only the sources are wanted here -- the built output is excluded
# below, from both the place it is produced and the place it is consumed.
!frontend/

# Re-excluded from inside the directories added above. `.venv` is the important
# one: it holds Linux-incompatible binaries when built on Windows or macOS, and
# copying it in would shadow the venv the image builds and fail at import with a
# message about a shared object rather than about the copy.
backend/**/.venv/
backend/**/__pycache__/
backend/**/*.py[cod]
backend/**/.pytest_cache/
backend/**/.ruff_cache/
backend/**/.mypy_cache/
backend/**/dist/

# **`backend/app/src/bacteria/app/console/` must NOT be listed here**, however
# much it looks like it belongs -- it is build output, and excluding build output
# is what the rest of this file does.
#
# This file is uploaded to FastAPI Cloud. `.gitignore` and `.fastapicloudignore`
# are stripped from the archive; `.dockerignore` and the `Dockerfile` are not, so
# the platform's builder reads this. Listing the console here excluded it from
# the deployed image: the API stayed healthy, every route kept working, and `/`
# answered 404 -- the silent failure `check_console_is_served` exists for, which
# is what caught it, twice, in sixty seconds.
#
# The Dockerfile gets its determinism by emptying that directory itself, just
# before copying the freshly built console in. See the `rm -rf` there.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/openapi.json

# Tests are not shipped. They need Postgres and dev dependencies the image does
# not install, so their presence would only be misleading.
backend/*/tests/

# Documentation and background reading. `articles/` and `pdfs/` are archived
# material that nothing imports and that would roughly double the image.
backend/*/docs/
backend/agent/articles/
backend/agent/pdfs/

# Never, under any circumstance. `.env` holds real provider credentials, and a
# layer that contains it keeps containing it after the file is deleted in a
# later layer.
.env
**/.env
